> Watch out. The ARM7 does not support this in direct assembler. If the
> compiler is not smart enough it would require a division, and that is
> really realy slow on a any ARM processor. 
> Helping the compiler by using
> 
> dreamcastcard->clicks &= 0x00000003;

Should be 7 instead of 3 :)


BTW, you don't have to restrict the buffer size and period size as
long as you have double-buffer, i.e. a buffer on CPU side and transfer
to the h/w buffer.  The only restricted parameter is the period size.
For example, a buffer with 13 periods can be mapped like:

BUF  0 ... 7 8 9 10 11 12 | 0 1 2 3 4 ...
H/W  0 ... 7 0 1 2  3  4  | 5 6 7 0 1 ...


